  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 147 AM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nDrier conditions are expected through Sunday morning but will not\nlast long as troughing over the western US amplifies and moves \ninto the central US. Models continue to struggle with the \nevolution of the trough as it moves into the Plains, with \nsolutions ranging from a slower, deeper cutoff low to more of an \nopen wave moving across our area. This will have implications \nfor rainfall amounts and severe weather potential, and obviously \ntiming, for our area. For now, the best model consensus would \nsuggest at least low end severe weather potential Monday into \nMonday night as moisture surges northward ahead of a \ndryline/pacific front, followed by cooler temperatures and perhaps\ncontinued shower activity Tuesday on the backside of the trough. \nHowever, given the uncertainty expect the details to continue to \nevolve as we draw closer. \n\nWare",
